WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.740
A pond skater stands on a pond.

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:06.520
Its legs dent the water,
but never break through.

3
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.400
Now watch a lake through
a day and a night.

4
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:12.800
The air above it warms and cools sharply.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.620
The lake water barely changes at all.

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.930
So how can weak attractions between
molecules hold up an insect,

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.420
and keep a lake's temperature steady?

8
00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:26.500
In this mission, you'll zoom in on the
water's surface to see what the insect

9
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.440
is really standing on.

10
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.450
Then you'll compare warming water and air:

11
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.940
for the same mass, water needs
about 4 times as much energy.

12
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:40.800
Your mission: explain how weak attractions
can hold up an insect and steady a

13
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.950
lake's temperature.
